{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Stores a flow command's entire body (the Case graph) and records the edit in the control's shared append-only patch journal (facet 'flow', with the command name; revert = write_flow_body of the entry's old body). Creates the flow command when it does not exist (returns created=true); errs if the name belongs to a non-flow command. Optional base hash from read_flow_body ⇒ stale_base on mismatch. Whole-body replace by design: the store re-serializes JSON canonically, so structured whole-body writes are the honest unit; text snippets are not (see the bench's flow3d design, review R-2).","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::time::time;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::system::unique_session_id::unique_session_id;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\n","params":[{"desc":"Library name.","name":"lib","type":"String"},{"desc":"Control name within the library.","name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"desc":"Flow command name on the control. Created (entry + record) when absent - this is how new flow commands are made; upsert_command is rust-only.","name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"desc":"The full Case graph to store, as JSON: {input, output, cmds, cons, nextcase?}. Every operation needs pos {x,y,z} and width; every terminal node needs mode, type, and x - the interpreter's parser requires them.","name":"body","type":"JSONObject"},{"desc":"Optional concurrency token: the hash from read_flow_body. Empty skips the check; stale ⇒ err stale_base with current_hash.","name":"base","type":"String"},{"desc":"Short human-readable label for the journal entry (e.g. 'wire params.a → +'). May be empty.","name":"label","type":"String"},{"desc":"Who is making the edit, recorded in the journal. May be empty.","name":"author","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"vksvyz19f99255185j789f","readers":[],"time":1786406017362,"username":"system","writers":[]}